Engineering Lead &lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hi 👋 we’re Genio. We create beautifully simple learning tools that boost knowledge, skills, and confidence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re a SaaS scale up and one of the fastest growing tech companies in the North.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;There’s 90+ of us around the UK with our HQ in Leeds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our software is award-winning and used by 100,000s of students at over 1,000 universities &amp;amp; colleges worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re growing so we can achieve our mission to support 1 million students to become better learners by 2030.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🚀&lt;strong&gt; About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career track:&lt;/strong&gt; MG4&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unit:&lt;/strong&gt; Learner Experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Engineering Lead you&#39;ll partner directly with the CPO to drive delivery, engineering standards, and team health as we build Genio&#39;s next flagship product. In this fast-paced, early-stage environment, you lead through empowerment rather than doing the work yourself; setting up your Tech Leads for success, fostering a culture of rapid AI-assisted experimentation, and ensuring problems are tackled early. Bringing sharp technical understanding to challenge assumptions and spot risk, you&#39;ll balance speed with smart standards to turn product priorities into shipped, learnable product.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will be responsible for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Run delivery for the Learning Experience team, from priority to shipped product. Ensure the team&#39;s delivery rhythm and visibility across planning, prioritisation, and release, keeping cycle times short and progress visible. Work with the CPO to translate product priorities and validation goals into sequenced engineering work, provide an honest view of what is achievable within the budget, remove blockers quickly, and ensure engineers are empowered to solve learner problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards and Ways of Working: &lt;/strong&gt;Bring genuine technical understanding to the team&#39;s engineering standards and ways of working, calibrated to a validation-stage product: fast by default, disciplined where it counts. Drive a culture of experimentation and fast feedback, champion AI-assisted engineering across the team, and ensure the team meets non-negotiable security and compliance standards set by Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Development &amp;amp; Culture:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage software engineers directly through regular 1-on-1s, development plans, performance management, and honest, timely feedback. Build a culture of collaboration, inclusiveness, trust, and respect. Coach team members on quality, communication, and best practices, address skill gaps, and take an active role in recruitment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Partnership: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with the Product Manager (who owns what and why) and Principal Engineer (who owns architecture), while owning the how and ensuring it ships. Bring genuine data proficiency so instrumentation, measurement, and learning are part of every release, and assist in communicating company goals and vision to provide clear direction for the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Outcomes:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast, dependable delivery:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;the team ships quickly and predictably, so product hypotheses are tested with real learners at the pace validation demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A culture of rapid iteration and experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;the team defaults to shipping, measuring, and learning, with AI-assisted development used wherever it compounds speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards that fit the stage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;quality, security, and engineering discipline are held where they matter, and deliberately lightweight where they don&#39;t yet, with trade-offs made consciously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A high-performing, motivated team:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;engineers are coached, developed, stretched, and supported, with clear expectations and honest feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A well-run budget:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;the team&#39;s size, tooling, and spend stay within what has been agreed, and the CPO always has a concrete view of what the current budget can deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;👥&lt;strong&gt; Meet the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be working most closely with our Chief Product Officer, Principal Engineer (Learning Experience), Tech Leads, Engineers, Senior Data Engineer, Learner Research and Design colleagues, Product Managers, and Principal Platform Engineer (Operations).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports directly into the Chief Product Officer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;👤 &lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Leadership Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Directly leading and managing engineers, ideally in an early-stage or new product environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Engineering Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep experience in hands-on software engineering roles, working with well-crafted and maintainable code, with sound judgement about when craft pays back and when speed wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Delivery Instincts:&lt;/strong&gt; Short cycles, visible progress, and honest communication when commitments are at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crisis-Capable: &lt;/strong&gt;Able to take ownership of a live problem end-to-end and see it through without escalating back or waiting for direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Genuine fluency with AI-assisted development and an appetite to push what it makes possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Proficiency: &lt;/strong&gt;Comfortable using product analytics and experiment results to steer the team&#39;s work, and able to bring Product Managers and others along in that reasoning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pragmatic Vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Long-term focused where it matters—supporting structures and habits that will scale if the platform succeeds, without investing prematurely in capabilities or abstractions that are not yet justified by validated needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;Passionate views, loosely held—able to argue your point of view passionately, but willing to accept that the needs of others, the group, or the business may mean other approaches are adopted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus / Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage-Appropriate Governance: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience balancing fast-paced product validation and experimentation with strict operational, security, and compliance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💰 Salary and benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;£115,000 - £125,000 dependent upon experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖️ 33 days annual leave (Inclusive of bank holidays)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎄 3 gifted days off at Christmas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 EMI Share Options Scheme&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎓 Generous individual learning and training allowance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⌚ Truly flexible hours to suit when you work best&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💻 Full home working set up and beautiful collaborative office space&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚗 Free Leeds City Centre office parking&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Nomad working policy with family travel insurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍼 Enhanced 26 weeks maternity and 4 weeks paternity (fully paid)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤍 Health cash plan (from glasses to massages)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💸 6% employer pension contribution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📍 Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our beautiful office space in Leeds is our key hub for collaboration, and we love to get together in person. We operate a flexible hybrid working model. While we don’t require a set number of days in the office, we’re happy to discuss ways of working at interview. If you have any questions in the meantime please reach out to &lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡 What to expect next:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll review your application and provide a response within 1 week. Even if it’s not the news you’d hoped for, we appreciate it’s good to know either way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If we invite you to meet with us for interview, here’s an overview of what the process will look like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening interview with someone in our Recruitment team (30 minutes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage one: interview with a small panel of interviewers including; the CEO, CPO, and another Genio colleague (1 hour). This will include a scenario with competency and behavioural questions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A take-home task to be completed ahead of the second stage interview, which will be presented during the interview.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage two: Task presentation and discussion, leadership focussed behavioural questions and an open conversation (90 minutes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final stage: Culture and values interview (1 hour)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ahead of your interview you will receive a confirmation email outlining who you’ll be meeting and when, anything you’ll need to prepare in advance and any resources we think you might find helpful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Engineering  Leeds

Director, International Privacy Lead and Data Protection Officer &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Director, International Privacy Lead &amp;amp; Data Protection Officer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alnylam is seeking an experienced privacy and data protection leader to serve as Director, International Privacy Lead &amp;amp; Data Protection Officer. Reporting to the Senior Director, Head of Privacy, AI Governance, Training &amp;amp; Communications within Ethics &amp;amp; Compliance, this role will lead Alnylam’s international privacy program, with primary responsibility for Europe (EU/EEA, United Kingdom, and Switzerland) and support for broader international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Alnylam’s formally appointed Data Protection Officer (DPO) under applicable European and Swiss privacy laws, the Director will provide independent privacy oversight, advise the business on data protection obligations, and maintain direct access and escalation channels to senior leadership for material privacy risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This individual contributor will be expected to serve as a proactive partner to the our international business, anticipating privacy and data protection obligations driven by regulatory change and business growth, and translating those requirements into actionable guidance for policies, operations and ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will partner closely with Legal, Information Security, IT, HR, Commercial, Medical Affairs, Clinical Development, Pharmacovigilance, Procurement, Ethics &amp;amp; Compliance, and other business stakeholders to enable responsible use of personal data while strengthening privacy governance, risk management, and business adoption across international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hybrid role preferably based in Zug, Switzerland.&amp;nbsp;Also open to candidates based in Madrid, Spain or Maidenhead, UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mature Alnylam’s international privacy program, with primary focus on Europe and support for broader international markets, by setting program priorities, strengthening governance frameworks, and ensuring privacy requirements are embedded into business planning, policies, controls, and day-to-day operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as Alnylam’s appointed DPO under EU GDPR, UK GDPR, and applicable Swiss data protection requirements, providing independent advice, monitoring compliance, maintaining required independence, and acting as the primary point of contact for supervisory authorities and data subjects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee privacy risk identification, assessment, mitigation, monitoring, and escalation processes, including privacy-by-design and privacy-by-default requirements, DPIAs, TIAs, Records of Processing Activities (ROPA), cross-border transfer assessments, and related governance documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise business and functional leaders on privacy requirements related to clinical research, pharmacovigilance, commercial operations, medical affairs, human resources, patient support programs, real-world evidence, AI, and other data-driven initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Information Security, Legal, Procurement, and business stakeholders on privacy incident response, breach assessment, third-party privacy risk management, data protection terms, data sharing arrangements, remediation, and regulatory notification decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively monitor the European and international privacy, AI, digital, cyber and data governance legislative landscape, anticipating compliance impacts from business growth and regulatory change, and rapidly translating new or changing requirements into practical updates to policies, controls, business processes, training, and operational guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver privacy training, communications, awareness initiatives, metrics, monitoring activities, and continuous improvement plans that promote a culture of privacy and accountability across international markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor (JD), LLM, or other advanced legal degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of privacy legal or compliance experience at a law firm and/or in-house.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience advising on privacy risk in regulated life sciences settings, including clinical research, pharmacovigilance, medical affairs, commercial, HR, patient-facing, and digital activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience serving as a DPO or advising in an equivalent independent oversight capacity for GDPR, UK GDPR, Swiss FADP, or comparable privacy regimes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of GDPR, UK GDPR, Swiss FADP, international data transfer requirements, and global privacy regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on AI, data-driven innovation, real-world evidence, cross-border data use, and other strategic privacy initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong privacy governance and risk management experience, including the ability to set priorities, mature program controls, and translate complex requirements into practical guidance for technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication, stakeholder management, and influencing skills, with the credibility and judgment to engage senior leaders, regulators, external partners, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex privacy initiatives across matrixed, international organizations, applying practical and proportionate judgment to ambiguous issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence, regulatory credibility, and strategic judgment to anticipate legal, business, and technology shifts and translate them into clear priorities for the international privacy program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Privacy certifications such as CIPP/E, CIPM, CIPT, AIGP, or similar credentials preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience interacting directly with European data protection authorities and regulators preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading multinational privacy teams or global privacy programs preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International business experience within a global life sciences organization preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Alnylam:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Alnylam Pharmaceuticals (Nasdaq: ALNY) has led the translation of RNA interference (RNAi) into a whole new class of innovative medicines with the potential to transform the lives of people afflicted with rare and more prevalent diseases. Based on Nobel Prize-winning science, RNAi therapeutics represent a powerful, clinically validated approach to treating diseases at their genetic source by “interfering” with mRNA that cause or contribute to disease. Since our founding in 2002, Alnylam has led the RNAi Revolution and continues to turn scientific possibility into reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our culture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Our people-first culture is guided by our core values: fiercely innovative, open culture, purposeful urgency, passion for excellence, and commitment to people, and these values influence how we work and the business decisions we make. Thanks to feedback from our employees over the years, we’ve been fortunate to be named a top employer around the world. Alnylam is extremely proud to have been recognized as one of Science Magazine’s Top Biopharma Employers, one of America&#39;s Most Responsible Companies for 2024 by Newsweek, a Fast Company Best Workplace for Innovators, and a Great Place to Work in Canada, France, Italy, Spain, Switzerland, and UK – among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alnylam, we commit to an inclusive recruitment process and equal employment opportunity. We are dedicated to building an environment where employees can feel that they belong, can bring their authentic selves to work, and achieve to their full potential. By empowering employees to embrace their unique differences at work, our business grows stronger with advanced and original thinking, allowing us to bring groundbreaking medicines to patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before applying, please review Alnylam&#39;s ⁠Candidate&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://alnylampolicies.com/&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;regarding how Alnylam handles Personal Data you provide with your application for employment.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Ethics and Compliance  Zug

Supply Chain Manager &lt;p&gt;As Supply Chain Manager, you will own, drive, and lead the end-to-end supply chain for Auterion products. This is a hands-on leadership role combining operational execution, people leadership, and strategic development of a resilient, scalable, and efficient supply chain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead and develop the supply chain team while working closely with Engineering, Procurement, Production, Logistics, Sales, Finance, and external partners. You will be the central point of ownership for supply chain performance, proactively identifying risks, solving issues, and driving improvements that support business growth and customer satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end supply chain for Auterion products, including supply planning, production scheduling, logistics, inventory, and order fulfilment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and grow the supply chain team, setting clear priorities, accountability, and ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive day-to-day execution and supply availability, ensuring materials, production requirements, shipments, inventory, and customer orders are managed accurately and on time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of escalation for supply disruptions, shortages, production constraints, and other supply chain risks, driving hands-on resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Procurement, suppliers, and logistics partners to improve delivery performance, lead times, reliability, capacity, quality, and resilience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement across supply chain processes, systems, data, and ways of working, including ERP and NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and monitor supply chain KPIs, using data to identify issues, drive corrective action, and provide clear recommendations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable processes and operating models, including SOPs, planning processes, and best practices to support business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional initiatives including new product introductions, engineering changes, supplier transitions, and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop supply chain strategy and resilience, including contingency planning, alternative sourcing, and critical-component strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the continued growth of the function through hiring, coaching, capability development, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in supply chain, procurement, logistics, planning, operations, or a related field, ideally in technology, hardware, aerospace, robotics, or manufacturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning and improving end-to-end supply chain processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading, mentoring, or developing people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of supply planning, procurement, inventory, production planning, logistics, and fulfilment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage risks, disruptions, shortages, and escalations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and data-driven decision-making skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP systems, ideally NetSuite, and strong Excel/spreadsheet skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and tracking KPIs and operational performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management and process improvement skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills across technical, operational, commercial, and leadership teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, pragmatic, proactive, and comfortable with autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident user of Google Workspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English required; German is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Global Operations  Munich

Tech Lead, Android Core Product - Toulouse, France &lt;p&gt;The mission of Speechify is to make sure that reading is never a barrier to learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 50 million people use Speechify’s text-to-speech products to turn whatever they’re reading – PDFs, books, Google Docs, news articles, websites – into audio, so they can read faster, read more, and remember more. Speechify’s text-to-speech reading products include its iOS app, Android App, Mac App, Chrome Extension, and Web App. Google recently named Speechify the Chrome Extension of the Year and Apple named Speechify its Design award winner for inclusivity for 2025.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, nearly 200 people around the globe work on Speechify in a 100% distributed setting – Speechify has no office. These include frontend and backend engineers, AI research scientists, and others from Amazon, Microsoft, and Google, leading PhD programs like Stanford, high growth startups like Stripe, Vercel, Bolt, and many founders of their own companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;With the growth of our Android app, being the most used text-to-speech app in the Play Store, we find the need for a Senior Android Engineer to help us support the new user base as well as work on new and exciting projects to push us forward. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;This is a key role and ideal for someone who thinks strategically, enjoys fast-paced environments, passionate about making product decisions, and has experience building great user experiences that delight users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;We are a flat organization that allows anyone to become a leader by showing excellent technical skills and delivering results consistently and fast. Work ethic, solid communication skills, and obsession with winning are paramount.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Our interview process involves several technical interviews and we aim to complete them within 1 week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Yo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;u’&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Owning major features and working closely with our design team - take ownership of features inside the app and become responsible of delivering high quality features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Shape the future of our Android team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Own, maintain and improve reliability metrics for key features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Participate in discussions across different teams - Product, Design, Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Review pull requests, and support other teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Handle critical issues or cope with unexpected challenges&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Take ownership of feature releases and provide nightly builds for the QA team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An Ideal Candidate Should Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with Android components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Experience building or contributing to at least one Android app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Product design intuition and user empathy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Drive to push the boundaries of Android UI/UX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Understanding of the importance of tests and how to approach writing tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Self-drive to improve the app and codebase above and beyond what&#39;s outlined in the spec&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Rock solid experience with Kotlin, Kotlin Coroutines, Kotlin Flow, Dagger 2, MVVM, Clean Architecture, Background Services, Music Player Service, Android Animations, Jetpack Navigation, JUnit tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;User oriented problem solving approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Driven with continuous feedback from leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Experience building, maintaining, or otherwise contributing to open source projects in Android&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Experience with iOS, Web or NodeJS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies we use:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Kotlin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Kotlin Coroutines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Kotlin Flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Jetpack Navigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Dagger 2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Custom Views, Canvas &amp;amp; Paint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;Jetpack Compose&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;JUnit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-speechify-sentence=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We offer&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fast-growing environment where you can help shape the company and product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial-minded team that supports risk, intuition, and hustle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-off management approach so you can focus and do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An opportunity to make a big impact in a transformative industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salaries, a friendly and laid-back atmosphere, and a commitment to building a great asynchronous culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on a life-changing product that millions of people use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build products that directly impact and support people with learning differences like dyslexia, ADD, low vision, concussions, autism, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in one of the fastest growing sectors of tech, the intersection of artificial intelligence and audio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The France Based &lt;/strong&gt;Salary range for this role is: 30,000-100,000 USD/Year + Bonus + Stock depending on experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think you’re a good fit for this job?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
